    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`, traced from the HTTP request to the response. The active profile is `h2,spring-data-jpa` with `petclinic.security.enable=false`, which matters for a couple of steps below.\n\n## Before the controller is even reached\n\n1. **Idempotency filter** (`OwnerIdempotencyFilter`, a servlet `OncePerRequestFilter` at `HIGHEST_PRECEDENCE`, so outermost). If the request carries an `Idempotency-Key` header that was seen before, it **replays the cached response body with status 200** and never enters the controller. Otherwise it wraps the response so it can cache a successful 201 later.\n\n2. **Security filter chain.** In the default profile `DisableSecurityConfig` is active \u2192 `permitAll`. Note the controller's `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` is **not enforced**, because `@EnableMethodSecurity` lives only on the (inactive) `BasicAuthenticationConfig`.\n\n3. **JSON deserialization** of the body into `OwnerFieldsDto` via the message converter.\n\n## RequestBodyAdvice chain (runs after deserialization, before `@Valid`)\n\nAll are `@ControllerAdvice` at `HIGHEST_PRECEDENCE`, so their **relative order is not deterministic**; the first to fail short-circuits with its own status. In effect:\n\n4. **Required fields** (`OwnerRequiredFieldsAdvice`) \u2014 rejects missing/blank `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`, and address (blank when both `address` and `addressLine1` are blank) \u2192 **400** `{\"errors\":[\u2026]}`.\n5. **Disposable email** (`OwnerDisposableEmailAdvice`) \u2014 rejects `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com` \u2192 **400**.\n6. **City capacity** (`OwnerCityCapacityAdvice`) \u2014 counts existing owners in the same (trimmed/lowercased) city; \u2265 50 \u2192 **409 Conflict**.\n7. **Daily limit** (`OwnerDailyLimitAdvice`) \u2014 counts owners with `registrationDate` == today's business day; \u2265 100 \u2192 **429 Too Many Requests**.\n8. **Telephone length** (`OwnerTelephoneLengthAdvice`) \u2014 normalizes to E.164 then checks national digit count (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210) \u2192 **400** on mismatch.\n9. **Postcode/region** (`OwnerPostcodeAdvice`) \u2014 if the 4-digit postcode is outside the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 **400**.\n10. **Future registration date** (`OwnerRegistrationDateAdvice`) \u2014 if supplied `registrationDate` is after `LocalDate.now()` \u2192 **400**.\n\n## Bean Validation\n\n11. **`@Valid` on `OwnerFieldsDto`** \u2014 `firstName`/`lastName` (`@NotNull @Pattern @Size 1\u201330`), `city` (`@NotNull @Size 1\u201380`), `telephone` (`@NotNull @Pattern \"10 digits\" @Size 1\u201320`), `email` (`@Size max 255 @Email`), `postcode` (`@Pattern ^[0-9]{4}$`), address fields (`@Size`). Failure \u2192 **400** `ProblemDetail` with `schemaValidationErrors` (via `ExceptionControllerAdvice`).\n\n## Controller \u2192 mapping side-effects (`OwnerMapper.toOwner`)\n\n12. **Telephone normalized to E.164** (`TelephoneNormalizer.toE164`; entity `setTelephone` re-applies it too).\n13. **`registrationDate` defaulted and rolled to a business day** \u2014 supplied date or `now()`, then `BusinessDays.toBusinessDay` rolls weekends/holidays forward.\n14. **Address composed and normalized** \u2014 `addressLine1/2`/`address` combined, trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, upper-cased, ST/RD/AVE expanded.\n15. **Email lower-cased** (entity `setEmail`). `id` and `pets` are left unset.\n\n## Service layer (`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`, `@Transactional`)\n\nFor a new owner (`id == null` and no customer code), against the full `findAll()` list, in this order:\n\n16. **Assign customer code** \u2014 `<REGION>-<HASH8>` where REGION is from postcode/city and HASH8 is SHA-256 over `telephone+lastName`, with `-<n>` suffix to de-duplicate.\n17. **Assign namesake count** \u2014 counts existing owners with same first+last (case-insensitive), then **household member count** (owners sharing `householdId`, +1).\n18. **Assign possible-duplicate** \u2014 `PossibleDuplicates.matchIn` currently **always returns null**, so this is always null on create.\n19. **Repository `save`** \u2192 Spring Data \u2192 `EntityManager.persist`; id is DB-generated (`@GeneratedValue IDENTITY`).\n20. **Hibernate re-validates entity constraints on flush** \u2014 `Person`/`Owner` `@NotEmpty` fields and `telephone` `@Pattern \"^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\"` (E.164). Failure \u2192 `ConstraintViolationException`.\n\nThere is **no password encoding** (BCrypt is only for users) and no timestamp beyond `registrationDate`.\n\n## After persistence\n\n21. **Audit log line** emitted (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber).\n22. **Response DTO built** (`toOwnerDto`) \u2014 derives many read-only fields (displayName, initials, membershipNumber/level/points, fiscalYear, locality/timezone, contactPreference, identityKey, checkDigit, ageBand, telephoneDisplay, selfLink).\n23. **Bulk-signup warning set** (`OwnerBulkSignupAdvice`, a `ResponseBodyAdvice`) \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = createdTodayCount() > 80`; informational only.\n24. **Response returned: 201 CREATED** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n25. **Idempotency filter caches** the 201 body if an `Idempotency-Key` was present, then writes the response.\n\n**A few things worth flagging:** the `@PreAuthorize` role check is dead in the default profile; the seven RequestBodyAdvice checks have no guaranteed ordering among themselves; the possible-duplicate check is a no-op; and the telephone/address/email/registrationDate values are silently transformed rather than validated, so what gets persisted can differ from what was submitted.\n\nWant me to dig into any single step (e.g. the exact customer-code hashing, or the business-day rolling logic)?"
